WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.360
At this point, virtually nobody on Earth scratches&nbsp;
their heads and wonders how it is that wealthy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:10.160
actors tend to look so fit and healthy. The answer&nbsp;
is simple: They have teams for that, and more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:14.560
often than not, they're in tip-top shape because&nbsp;
they're being paid to do so. When it's time to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:19.680
absolutely shredded for their latest action movie,&nbsp;
actors assemble their fitness Avengers: exercises&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:24.720
coaches, nutritionists, stuntmen with years of&nbsp;
experience, professional mixed martial artists,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:29.360
and anyone else who might be able to take an&nbsp;
already in-shape body to the superhuman level.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:32.480
There are very few actors out there&nbsp;
as ripped as Chris Hemsworth is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:35.680
which makes sense considering who&nbsp;
he plays in the Marvel Cinematic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:39.040
Universe. It's one thing to be a&nbsp;
super-soldier like Steve Rogers…

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:41.680
“As far as I’m concerned, that is America’s ass.”

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:46.320
or an intergalactic guardian like Peter&nbsp;
Quill, but it's quite another to be Thor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:51.040
the Asgardian god of thunder. And while Thor was&nbsp;
in a very different kind of shape by Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:54.080
Endgame, looking rounder around&nbsp;
the middle and longer in the beard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:57.520
Hemsworth in real life tends&nbsp;
to keep himself pretty jacked.

00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:58.960
“Strongest Avenger.”

00:00:58.960 --> 00:00:59.760
“Access denied.”

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.160
“STRONGEST AVENGER.”

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:02.960
“Access denied.”

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:08.320
Recently, Hemsworth decided to get&nbsp;
into the app business and create Centr,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:12.000
a pay-to-use app that makes his team&nbsp;
of fitness professionals your team&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.800
too, with customized meal plans and workout&nbsp;
regimens to help you reach your health goals.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:21.200
And what better way to promote Centr than to&nbsp;
post a hilarious ad that blends Hemsworth's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:26.412
unfiltered Aussie humor with his dedication&nbsp;
to fitness and his personal team's expertise?

00:01:26.412 --> 00:01:30.880
"And allow my soothing baritones&nbsp;
to wash over you. I love you."

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:34.800
Hemsworth took to Instagram on March 23rd to share&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:38.480
the ad with his 47 million-plus&nbsp;
followers. It features a number&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:42.960
of people working out ... who all just so&nbsp;
happen to be the actor himself — sort of.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:47.760
In the video, Hemsworth's head appears over the&nbsp;
bodies of a number of people, most of whom are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:52.400
dedicating themselves towards some kind of&nbsp;
physical or mental wellness — working out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:57.520
doing yoga, meditating, and so on... Hemsworth&nbsp;
speaks all the dialogue, discussing in very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:02.400
colorful terms how unlikable he is and how awesome&nbsp;
the people who work with him are. In Hemsworth's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:06.880
words, he's a "f-----g d--k" and his team is&nbsp;
"f-----g brilliant." Two women — who, again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:11.520
both have Hemsworth's face — discuss how they&nbsp;
prefer Chris' brother Luke, for example, and a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:16.400
guy cooking things up on the grill confesses he'd&nbsp;
rip off Chris Hemsworth's face in a cage match.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:20.000
Those who've kept up with Hemsworth's&nbsp;
personal and professional endeavors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:24.880
will recognize this new clip as an uncensored&nbsp;
version of a Centr ad that ran in February.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:29.200
It's the same premise — Hemsworth's head&nbsp;
superimposed over other people's bodies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:32.800
him saying that working out with his&nbsp;
team is basically like working out with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:36.960
him — but with updated dialogue not fit&nbsp;
for little ears. It ends with the tag,

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:40.000
"You don't have to be Chris to get&nbsp;
results. You just need his team."

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:44.080
The point of that ad is that, whether you love&nbsp;
or hate Chris Hemsworth, something most of us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:48.640
can likely agree on is that he clearly has an&nbsp;
excellent team keeping him in shape. That's where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:54.000
Centr comes in; it's a wellness program Hemsworth&nbsp;
curated that includes a number of experts he's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:58.480
used over the years to get into the kind of shape&nbsp;
required for the different roles he's taken.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:04.640
Boxers, gold medal-winning gymnasts, yogis, chefs,&nbsp;
and even podcasting therapists make up the squad.

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:08.720
Hemsworth is currently putting the fruits&nbsp;
of his fitness labors to use to film Thor:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:12.320
Love and Thunder, the fourth solo&nbsp;
film centered on the God of Thunder.

